comment17.text=\r\n Should not change the symbols of the wheels if the symbol doesn't exist.\r\n
comment18.target=void shouldSpinJustASpecificWheel()
comment18.text=\r\n Should spin a specific wheel's symbol.\r\n
comment19.target=void shouldSpinLastWheelIfPosTooBig()
comment19.text=\r\n If we spin a specific wheel in a position bigger than the number of wheels, we should spin the last one.\r\n
comment2.target=void shouldWheelNumberBeGreaterIfWheelAdded()
comment2.text=\r\n If a wheel is added, the number of wheels should be greater\r\n
comment20.target=void shouldSpinFirstWheelIfPosTooShort()
comment20.text=\r\n If we spin a specific wheel in a position lower than the number of wheels, we should spin the first one.\r\n
comment21.target=void shouldChangeAllWheelsSymbols()
comment21.text=\r\n If we do spin to all the wheels it should change their symbols.\r\n
comment22.target=void shouldGiveCorrectDistinctSymbolsNumber()
comment22.text=\r\n If we put a set of symbols it should give us how many different symbols are.\r\n
comment23.target=void shouldGiveCorrectCurrentSymbols()
comment23.text=\r\n If we put a set of symbols configuration should give us those current symbols.\r\n
comment24.target=void shouldBeJackpotIfAllSymbolsAreEquals()
comment24.text=\r\n If all symbols are equals we should win.\r\n
comment25.target=void shouldNotBeJackpotIfAtLeastTwoSymbolsAreDifferent()
comment25.text=\r\n If at least two symbols are different we shouldn't win.\r\n
comment26.target=void tearDown()
comment26.text=\r\n Tears down the test fixture.\r\n
comment3.target=void shouldAddWheelAtEndIfPosTooBig()
